    "lawCode": "Add §346, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4155\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to commuter van classi-\nfication review\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require the Department of Financial services to review the classi-\nfication used by insurers issuing auto insurance coverage to commuter\nvans.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill would, add a new section 344 to the insurance\nlaw. This section would require the Superintendent of the Department of\nFinancial Services to conduct a review of the classification used by\nauthorized insurers issuing auto insurance coverage to commuter vans.\n\nThis review shall include:\n\n* Whether the assumed risks used in the calculation of premiums for\ncommuter vans by insurers are appropriate;\n\n* Whether the current classification and risk assessment of commuter\nvans by insurers is the most cost-effective classification based on the\nassumed risks, if another classification could be more cost effective,\nand a detailed analysis of the reason or reasons for such differences in\ncosts and the average amount of difference in costs; and\n\n*The cost differential between the premium for being classified as\n\"other buses\" by insurers, and the premium for being classified as a\ncommuter van where such premium is based solely on the risks specific to\ncommuter vans in such plan.\n\nThis section would also require the Superintendent to make a determi-\nnation, after the review, of whether a new classification for commuter\nvans should be created and if so, require insurers to use such new clas-\nsification.\n\nThis section would also require the Superintendent to complete the\nreview within 90 days of the effective date of this act and submit a\nreport of the superintendent's findings and determinations to the gover-\nnor, the legislature and the chairs of the Senate and Assembly insurance\ncommittees within 60 days after completing such review.  Section two of\nthe bill would provide the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAuto insurers often place individuals or entities with similar risk\ncharacteristics into groups or classes for the purpose of underwriting\npolicies and determining appropriate premium rates.Currently, commuter\nvans are placed in the same classification as other types of passenger\nbuses such as urban buses, charter buses and sightseeing buses. Concerns\nhave been raised that this classification has resulted in steep annual\npremium increases for commuter van coverage due to the fact that the\nrisks of commuter vans are combined with the risks of other types of\nbuses which often carry a larger number of passengers and travel greater\ndistances than commuter vans.\n\nThis bill seeks to address these concerns by requiring the superinten-\ndent of the department of financial services to review the current clas-\nsification of commuter vans used by authorized insurers and determine\nwhether a new classification should be created and if so, to require\ninsurers to use such new classification.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
